    `earnings because of which, under section 19 of the Act, no benefits are payable received or to be received`                                       IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)(iv); out of range: s 19 of the Act (piece ei1)
    `attending a course or program of instruction or training to which the claimant was referred by the Commission or a designated authority`           IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(i)
    `employed under the Self-employment or Job Creation Partnerships employment benefit or a similar benefit under an agreement under section 63`      IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(ii); out of range: ss 59 and 63 of the Act (piece ei2)
    `prevented from establishing an interruption of earnings by the allocation of earnings under section 36`                                            IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(iii); out of range: reg 36 (piece er3)
    `serving a week of the waiting period`                                                                                                              IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(iv); out of range: s 13 of the Act, the waiting period (piece ei1)
    `disqualified`                                                                                                                                      IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(v); out of range: ss 6(1) and 30 of the Act, disqualification (pieces ei1, ei2)
    `a week of unemployment due to a stoppage of work attributable to a labour dispute at the premises at which the claimant was employed`              IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)

§ `Part I -- section 6.1: a week of very low earnings (applies 30 June to 31 December 1996)`

-- "20 per cent of the maximum weekly insurable earnings": the amount of cash earnings referred to in subsection (1).
-- src:2248 | 6.1 (1) Subject to subsection (2), the employment with an employer in any week of a person whose cash earnings are less than 20 per cent of the maximum weekly insurable earnings and who is employed for less than 15 hours is excluded from insurable employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part I s 6.1(1) (src:2248)
GIVEN `the maximum weekly insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: Act Schedule II item 1, interim s 4(2) (piece ei6): $750, no year named
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the amount of cash earnings` MEANS (20%) TIMES `the maximum weekly insurable earnings`

-- (2): where the earnings for a pay period "are paid or payable ... otherwise than in respect of weeks", subsection (1) does not apply
-- to the employment in that pay period if the pay period is one of the five kinds and earns or works enough for it.
-- src:2249 | (2) Where the cash earnings of a person for a pay period described in any of the following paragraphs are paid or payable to the person otherwise than in respect of weeks, subsection (1) does not apply to the employment of that person during any such pay period:
-- src:2250 | (a) a pay period that is a multiple of a week where
-- src:2251 | (i) the person has cash earnings for each week in the pay period, and the cash earnings for the pay period are equal to or exceed an amount that is a like multiple of the amount of cash earnings referred to in subsection (1), or
-- src:2252 | (ii) the person is employed in each week in the pay period and the total number of hours of employment in the pay period is equal to or exceeds a number of hours that is a like multiple of 15;
-- src:2253 | (b) a pay period that is a semi-monthly pay period where
-- src:2254 | (i) the person has cash earnings for each week or part of a week that falls in the pay period, and the cash earnings for the pay period are equal to or exceed an amount that is 2 1/6 times the amount of cash earnings referred to in subsection (1), or
-- src:2255 | (ii) the person is employed in each week or part of a week that falls in the pay period, and the total number of hours of employment in the pay period is 33 hours or more;
-- src:2256 | (c) a pay period that is a monthly pay period where
-- src:2257 | (i) the person has cash earnings for each week or part of a week that falls in the pay period, and the cash earnings for the pay period are equal to or exceed an amount that is 4 1/3 times the amount of cash earnings referred to in subsection (1), or
-- src:2258 | (ii) the person is employed in each week or part of a week that falls in the pay period, and the total number of hours of employment in the pay period is 65 hours or more;
-- src:2259 | (d) a pay period of seven consecutive days that begins on a day other than Sunday, where
-- src:2260 | (i) the person has cash earnings for the pay period and the cash earnings for the pay period are equal to or exceed 20 per cent of the maximum weekly insurable earnings, or
-- src:2261 | (ii) the person is employed in the pay period for a total number of hours that is equal to or exceeds 15 hours; or
-- src:2262 | (e) a pay period that consists of more than one period of seven consecutive days and that begins on a day other than Sunday, where
-- src:2263 | (i) the person has cash earnings for each period of seven consecutive days in the pay period, and the cash earnings for the pay period are equal to or exceed the product obtained by multiplying the amount of cash earnings referred to in subsection (1) by the number of periods of seven consecutive days in the pay period, or
-- src:2264 | (ii) the person is employed in each period of seven consecutive days in the pay period and the total number of hours of employment in the pay period is equal to or exceeds the product obtained by multiplying 15 by the number of periods of seven consecutive days in the pay period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part I s 6.1(2) (src:2249-2264)
GIVEN period IS AN `er6 Pay period`
      facts IS AN `er6 Earnings and hours in a pay period`
      `the maximum weekly insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` IF
    CONSIDER period
    WHEN `er6 a multiple of a week` n THEN
            (    facts's `cash earnings for each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period`
             AND facts's `cash earnings for the pay period` AT LEAST n TIMES `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the amount of cash earnings` `the maximum weekly insurable earnings`)   -- (a)(i): a like multiple of the amount
         OR (    facts's `employment in each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period`
             AND facts's `total number of hours of employment in the pay period` AT LEAST n TIMES 15)   -- (a)(ii): a like multiple of 15
    WHEN `er6 a semi-monthly pay period` THEN
            (    facts's `cash earnings for each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period`
             AND facts's `cash earnings for the pay period` AT LEAST (2 PLUS (1 DIVIDED BY 6)) TIMES `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the amount of cash earnings` `the maximum weekly insurable earnings`)   -- (b)(i): 2 1/6 times
         OR (    facts's `employment in each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period`
             AND facts's `total number of hours of employment in the pay period` AT LEAST 33)   -- (b)(ii)
    WHEN `er6 a monthly pay period` THEN
            (    facts's `cash earnings for each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period`
             AND facts's `cash earnings for the pay period` AT LEAST (4 PLUS (1 DIVIDED BY 3)) TIMES `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the amount of cash earnings` `the maximum weekly insurable earnings`)   -- (c)(i): 4 1/3 times
         OR (    facts's `employment in each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period`
             AND facts's `total number of hours of employment in the pay period` AT LEAST 65)   -- (c)(ii)
    WHEN `er6 seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` THEN
            facts's `cash earnings for the pay period` AT LEAST `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the amount of cash earnings` `the maximum weekly insurable earnings`   -- (d)(i): 20 per cent of the maximum weekly insurable earnings
         OR facts's `total number of hours of employment in the pay period` AT LEAST 15   -- (d)(ii)
    WHEN `er6 more than one period of seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` n THEN
            (    facts's `cash earnings for each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period`
             AND facts's `cash earnings for the pay period` AT LEAST `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the amount of cash earnings` `the maximum weekly insurable earnings` TIMES n)   -- (e)(i): the amount times the number of periods
         OR (    facts's `employment in each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period`
             AND facts's `total number of hours of employment in the pay period` AT LEAST 15 TIMES n)   -- (e)(ii)

-- src:2248 | 6.1 (1) Subject to subsection (2), the employment with an employer in any week of a person whose cash earnings are less than 20 per cent of the maximum weekly insurable earnings and who is employed for less than 15 hours is excluded from insurable employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part I s 6.1(1) (src:2248)
GIVEN day IS A DATE   -- a day in the week
      `the person’s cash earnings in the week` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of hours the person is employed in the week` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum weekly insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `subsection (2) says that subsection (1) does not apply to the pay period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the employment in the week is excluded from insurable employment` IF
        `reg 95(4) the provision set out in Part I of Schedule III applies on the day` day
    AND `the person’s cash earnings in the week` LESS THAN `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the amount of cash earnings` `the maximum weekly insurable earnings`
    AND `the number of hours the person is employed in the week` LESS THAN 15
    AND NOT (`subsection (2) says that subsection (1) does not apply to the pay period`)

§ `Part I.1 -- section 12: prescribed weeks (applies 12 September to 31 December 1996)`

-- src:2270 | 12 (1) For the purposes of paragraph 7(4)(c) of the Act, a prescribed week is:
-- src:2271 | (a) a week in respect of which a claimant has received or will receive
-- src:2272 | (i) workers’ compensation payments, other than a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement of a claim made for workers’ compensation payments,
-- src:2273 | (ii) under a wage-loss indemnity plan, any earnings by reason of illness, injury, quarantine, pregnancy or care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) of the Act,
-- src:2274 | (iii) indemnity payments referred to in paragraph 35(2)(f), or
-- src:2275 | (iv) earnings because of which, pursuant to section 19 of the Act, no benefits are payable to the claimant;
-- src:2276 | (b) a week in which the claimant was
-- src:2277 | (i) attending a course or program of instruction or training to which the claimant was referred by the Commission or by an authority designated by the Commission,
-- src:2278 | (ii) employed under the Self-employment employment benefit or the Job Creation Partnerships employment benefit established by the Commission under section 59 of the Act or under a similar benefit that is provided by a provincial government or other organization and is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act,
-- src:2279 | (iii) prevented from establishing an interruption of earnings by virtue of the allocation of earnings pursuant to section 36,
-- src:2280 | (iv) serving a week of the waiting period, or
-- src:2281 | (v) disqualified; or
-- src:2282 | (c) a week of unemployment due to a stoppage of work attributable to a labour dispute at the factory, workshop or other premises at which the claimant was employed.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part I.1 s 12(1) (src:2270-2282)
GIVEN day IS A DATE   -- a day in the week
      facts IS AN `er6 Facts about a week`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(1) the week is a prescribed week for the purposes of paragraph 7(4)(c) of the Act` IF
        `reg 95(4.1) the provision set out in Part I.1 of Schedule III applies in place of section 12 on the day` day
    AND (   facts's `workers’ compensation payments received or to be received, other than a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement of a claim`   -- (a)(i)
         OR facts's `earnings under a wage-loss indemnity plan by reason of illness, injury, quarantine, pregnancy or care of a child received or to be received`   -- (a)(ii)
         OR facts's `indemnity payments referred to in paragraph 35(2)(f) received or to be received`   -- (a)(iii)
         OR facts's `earnings because of which, under section 19 of the Act, no benefits are payable received or to be received`   -- (a)(iv)
         OR facts's `attending a course or program of instruction or training to which the claimant was referred by the Commission or a designated authority`   -- (b)(i)
         OR facts's `employed under the Self-employment or Job Creation Partnerships employment benefit or a similar benefit under an agreement under section 63`   -- (b)(ii)
         OR facts's `prevented from establishing an interruption of earnings by the allocation of earnings under section 36`   -- (b)(iii)
         OR facts's `serving a week of the waiting period`   -- (b)(iv)
         OR facts's `disqualified`   -- (b)(v)
         OR facts's `a week of unemployment due to a stoppage of work attributable to a labour dispute at the premises at which the claimant was employed`)   -- (c)

-- (2): "where a week is taken into account under any paragraph or subparagraph of that subsection, that week may not be taken into account under any other":
-- the weeks are counted, not the paragraphs, so a week that meets two of them counts once.
-- src:2283 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), where a week is taken into account under any paragraph or subparagraph of that subsection, that week may not be taken into account under any other paragraph or subparagraph of that subsection.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part I.1 s 12(2) (src:2283)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      weeks IS A LIST OF `er6 Facts about a week`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(2) the number of prescribed weeks, each week taken into account once` IS
    count (filter (GIVEN w YIELD `Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(1) the week is a prescribed week for the purposes of paragraph 7(4)(c) of the Act` day w) weeks)

§ `Part II item 2 -- sections 19 and 20: the record of employment (applies 30 June to 31 December 1996)`

-- 19(1): "Every employer who employs a person in insurable employment shall, if that person has an interruption of earnings, complete a
-- record of employment in quadruplicate ... on a form supplied by the Commission." The duty is the employer's; the right to the record is the insured person's.
-- src:2289 | 19 (1) Every employer who employs a person in insurable employment shall, if that person has an interruption of earnings, complete a record of employment in quadruplicate with respect to that person on a form supplied by the Commission.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part II s 19(1) (src:2289)
GIVEN day IS A DATE   -- the first day of the interruption of earnings
      `the employer employs the person in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN   -- the core's s 5 (keel)
      `the person has an interruption of earnings` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: reg 14 (piece er1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch III Part II s 19(1) the employer must complete a record of employment` IF
        `reg 95(5) the provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 19 to 21 on the day` day
    AND `the employer employs the person in insurable employment`
    AND `the person has an interruption of earnings`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part II s 19(1) (src:2289)
`Regs Sch III Part II s 19(1) the number of copies of the record of employment` MEANS 4   -- "in quadruplicate"

-- 19(2)(a) and (b): the employee's copies are delivered or mailed to the insured person, and the Commission's copy is mailed, "not later than five days
-- after the later of (i) the first day of the interruption of earnings, and (ii) the day on which the employer becomes aware of the interruption of earnings".
-- src:2290 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), copies of the record of employment completed pursuant to subsection (1) shall be distributed in the following manner:
-- src:2291 | (a) the copies marked “Employee’s copy: Part 1” and “Employee’s copy: Part 2” shall be delivered or mailed to the insured person not later than five days after the later of
-- src:2292 | (i) the first day of the interruption of earnings, and
-- src:2293 | (ii) the day on which the employer becomes aware of the interruption of earnings;
-- src:2294 | (b) the copy marked “Commission’s copy” shall be mailed to the Commission within the time limit set out in paragraph (a); and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part II s 19(2)(a) and (b) (src:2290-2294)
GIVEN `the first day of the interruption of earnings` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the employer becomes aware of the interruption of earnings` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Regs Sch III Part II s 19(2) the last day for delivering or mailing the copies of the record of employment` IS
    IF `reg 95(5) the provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 19 to 21 on the day` `the first day of the interruption of earnings`
    THEN JUST (`the last day of` 5 `days after`
                (IF `the first day of the interruption of earnings` AT LEAST `the day on which the employer becomes aware of the interruption of earnings`
                 THEN `the first day of the interruption of earnings`
                 ELSE `the day on which the employer becomes aware of the interruption of earnings`))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 19(2)(c): the employer's copy "shall be kept and retained as a part of the employer's records and books of account in accordance with subsection 87(3) of the Act"
-- (out of range: s 87(3) of the Act, piece ei3, says how long; the duty here carries no date of its own).
-- src:2295 | (c) the copy marked “Employer’s copy” shall be kept and retained as a part of the employer’s records and books of account in accordance with subsection 87(3) of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part II s 19(2)(c) (src:2295)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch III Part II s 19(2)(c) the employer must keep the employer’s copy with its records and books of account` IF
    `reg 95(5) the provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 19 to 21 on the day` day

-- 19(3): "If, for reasons beyond the employer's control, the employer is unable to deliver or mail the [employee's] copies ... within the time limit
-- set out in paragraph (2)(a), the employer shall retain them until (a) such time as they are requested by the Commission or insured person, or
-- (b) 52 weeks after the time limit set out in paragraph (2)(a), whichever is earlier."
-- src:2296 | (3) If, for reasons beyond the employer’s control, the employer is unable to deliver or mail the copies marked “Employee’s copy: Part 1” and “Employee’s copy: Part 2” of the completed record of employment to the insured person within the time limit set out in paragraph (2)(a), the employer shall retain them until
-- src:2297 | (a) such time as they are requested by the Commission or insured person, or
-- src:2298 | (b) 52 weeks after the time limit set out in paragraph (2)(a),
-- src:2299 | whichever is earlier.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part II s 19(3) (src:2296-2299)
GIVEN `the last day of the time limit set out in paragraph (2)(a)` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the Commission or the insured person requests the copies` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Regs Sch III Part II s 19(3) the day until which the employer retains the employee’s copies` IS
    IF NOT (`reg 95(5) the provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 19 to 21 on the day` `the last day of the time limit set out in paragraph (2)(a)`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (CONSIDER `the day on which the Commission or the insured person requests the copies`
               WHEN NOTHING THEN `the end of the 52 weeks`
               WHEN JUST requested THEN
                   IF requested AT MOST `the end of the 52 weeks` THEN requested ELSE `the end of the 52 weeks`)
    WHERE
        `the end of the 52 weeks` MEANS `the last day of the time limit set out in paragraph (2)(a)` PLUS (`weeks as days` 52)

-- 19(4): the weeks and earnings reported are those "as determined and allocated pursuant to Parts III and IV of the Act and any regulations made under those Parts,
-- but sections 35 and 36 of these Regulations shall not apply in respect of any such determination".
-- src:2300 | (4) The number of weeks of insurable employment and insurable earnings reported in a record of employment with respect to an insured person shall be as determined and allocated pursuant to Parts III and IV of the Act and any regulations made under those Parts, but sections 35 and 36 of these Regulations shall not apply in respect of any such determination.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part II s 19(4) (src:2300)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch III Part II s 19(4) sections 35 and 36 of these Regulations do not apply to the determination of the weeks and earnings reported in a record of employment` IF
    `reg 95(5) the provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 19 to 21 on the day` day

-- 19(5): "Where the earnings of a claimant for a pay period that is current when the claimant has a lay-off or separation from employment cannot be ascertained
-- with accuracy, the employer may estimate the earnings for that period."
-- src:2301 | (5) Where the earnings of a claimant for a pay period that is current when the claimant has a lay-off or separation from employment cannot be ascertained with accuracy, the employer may estimate the earnings for that period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part II s 19(5) (src:2301)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the pay period is current when the claimant has a lay-off or separation from employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earnings for that pay period cannot be ascertained with accuracy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch III Part II s 19(5) the employer may estimate the earnings for the pay period` IF
        `reg 95(5) the provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 19 to 21 on the day` day
    AND `the pay period is current when the claimant has a lay-off or separation from employment`
    AND `the earnings for that pay period cannot be ascertained with accuracy`

-- 20(1): the claimant's power to give a statement in place of the record.
-- src:2302 | 20 (1) Where an employer has failed to deliver a record of employment to an insured person or the Commission pursuant to section 19 or the employer is not available or is unable to provide information respecting the employment history and insurable earnings of a claimant because the employer’s records are destroyed or lost, a claimant may provide a statement containing evidence of their employment history and insurable earnings.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part II s 20(1) (src:2302)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the employer has failed to deliver a record of employment to the insured person or the Commission under section 19` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is not available or is unable to provide the information because its records are destroyed or lost` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch III Part II s 20(1) the claimant may provide a statement containing evidence of their employment history and insurable earnings` IF
        `reg 95(5) the provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 19 to 21 on the day` day
    AND (   `the employer has failed to deliver a record of employment to the insured person or the Commission under section 19`
         OR `the employer is not available or is unable to provide the information because its records are destroyed or lost`)

-- 20(2): "All the weeks of insurable employment reported in a record of employment shall be determined to have occurred consecutively and to be weeks that
-- immediately preceded and included the week in which the lay-off or separation occurred." So n weeks end with the week of the lay-off: the first of them begins 7 (n - 1) days before it.
-- src:2303 | (2) All the weeks of insurable employment reported in a record of employment shall be determined to have occurred consecutively and to be weeks that immediately preceded and included the week in which the lay-off or separation occurred.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part II s 20(2) (src:2303)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the Sunday that begins the week in which the lay-off or separation occurred` IS A DATE
      `the number of weeks of insurable employment reported` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Regs Sch III Part II s 20(2) the Sunday that begins the first of the weeks of insurable employment` IS
    IF `reg 95(5) the provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 19 to 21 on the day` day
    THEN JUST (`the Sunday that begins the week in which the lay-off or separation occurred` MINUS (`weeks as days` (`the number of weeks of insurable employment reported` MINUS 1)))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 20(3): "Notwithstanding subsection 19(4) and section 23, for the purposes of Part I of the Act, the number of weeks of insurable employment in any one employment
-- period of a claimant shall not be greater than the number of weeks or part weeks that falls within that employment period."
-- src:2304 | (3) Notwithstanding subsection 19(4) and section 23, for the purposes of Part I of the Act, the number of weeks of insurable employment in any one employment period of a claimant shall not be greater than the number of weeks or part weeks that falls within that employment period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part II s 20(3) (src:2304)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the number of weeks of insurable employment reported in the employment period` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks or part weeks that fall within the employment period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Regs Sch III Part II s 20(3) the number of weeks of insurable employment in the employment period` IS
    IF `reg 95(5) the provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 19 to 21 on the day` day
    THEN JUST (IF `the number of weeks of insurable employment reported in the employment period` AT MOST `the number of weeks or part weeks that fall within the employment period`
               THEN `the number of weeks of insurable employment reported in the employment period`
               ELSE `the number of weeks or part weeks that fall within the employment period`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 20(4): "Where a bankrupt employer or the trustee of the bankrupt employer has not provided the Commission with a record of employment for an insured person, the
-- Commission may, in respect of that person, determine the number of insurable weeks and the amount of insurable earnings for benefit purposes on the basis of the payroll and
-- personnel records of the bankrupt employer provided to the Commission by the trustee." What this means for the person: the Commission may rely on the trustee's records.
-- src:2305 | (4) Where a bankrupt employer or the trustee of the bankrupt employer has not provided the Commission with a record of employment for an insured person, the Commission may, in respect of that person, determine the number of insurable weeks and the amount of insurable earnings for benefit purposes on the basis of the payroll and personnel records of the bankrupt employer provided to the Commission by the trustee.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part II s 20(4) (src:2305)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the employer is bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `neither the employer nor its trustee has provided the Commission with a record of employment for the insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustee has provided the Commission with the payroll and personnel records of the bankrupt employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch III Part II s 20(4) the Commission may determine the insurable weeks and insurable earnings from the trustee’s payroll and personnel records` IF
        `reg 95(5) the provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 19 to 21 on the day` day
    AND `the employer is bankrupt`
    AND `neither the employer nor its trustee has provided the Commission with a record of employment for the insured person`
    AND `the trustee has provided the Commission with the payroll and personnel records of the bankrupt employer`

§ `Part II item 3 -- sections 22 and 23: earnings and weeks counted (applies 30 June 1996 to 4 January 1997)`

-- src:2307 | 22 The earnings to be taken into account for the purpose of determining the average weekly insurable earnings for the purposes of section 14 of the Act as set out in section 6 of Schedule II to the Act are those earnings for which a premium was payable.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part II s 22 (src:2307)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `a premium was payable on the earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch III Part II s 22 the earnings are taken into account in determining the average weekly insurable earnings` IF
        `reg 95(5) the provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c) on the day` day
    AND `a premium was payable on the earnings`

-- s 23: where the earnings were paid or payable in the qualifying period "for a period otherwise than in respect of weeks (hereinafter called the 'pay period')",
-- the weeks taken as weeks of insurable employment in an employment period equal (a) the number of pay periods, for a pay period of seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than
-- Sunday that earns 20 per cent of the maximum weekly insurable earnings or has 15 hours, and (b) the number of periods of seven days, for a longer such pay period that earns that amount, or has that many hours, for each.
-- src:2308 | 23 For the purposes of Part I of the Act, where a claimant’s earnings were paid or payable in the qualifying period for a period otherwise than in respect of weeks (hereinafter called the “pay period”), the number of weeks that are to be taken as weeks of insurable employment in any one employment period shall
-- src:2309 | (a) where the pay period consists of seven consecutive days and begins on a day other than Sunday and
-- src:2310 | (i) the claimant has cash earnings for each pay period and the cash earnings for the pay period are equal to or exceed 20 per cent of the maximum weekly insurable earnings, or
-- src:2311 | (ii) the claimant is employed in each pay period for a total number of hours that is equal to or exceeds 15 hours,
-- src:2312 | be equal to the number of pay periods; and
-- src:2313 | (b) where the pay period consists of more than one period of seven consecutive days and begins on a day other than Sunday and
-- src:2314 | (i) the claimant has cash earnings for each period of seven consecutive days in the pay period, and the cash earnings for the pay period are equal to or exceed the product obtained by multiplying the amount of cash earnings referred to in paragraph (a) by the number of periods of seven consecutive days in the pay period, or
-- src:2315 | (ii) the claimant is employed in each period of seven consecutive days in the pay period, and the total number of hours of employment in the pay period is equal to or exceeds the product obtained by multiplying 15 by the number of periods of seven consecutive days in the pay period,
-- src:2316 | be equal to the number of periods of seven consecutive days in the pay period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part II s 23 (src:2308-2316)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      period IS AN `er6 Pay period`
      facts IS AN `er6 Earnings and hours in a pay period`
      `the number of pay periods` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum weekly insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Regs Sch III Part II s 23 the number of weeks that are to be taken as weeks of insurable employment` IS
    IF NOT (`reg 95(5) the provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c) on the day` day)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER period
         WHEN `er6 seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` THEN
             IF    (    facts's `cash earnings for each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period`
                    AND facts's `cash earnings for the pay period` AT LEAST `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the amount of cash earnings` `the maximum weekly insurable earnings`)   -- (a)(i)
                OR (    facts's `employment in each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period`
                    AND facts's `total number of hours of employment in the pay period` AT LEAST 15)   -- (a)(ii)
             THEN JUST `the number of pay periods`
             ELSE NOTHING
         WHEN `er6 more than one period of seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` n THEN
             IF    (    facts's `cash earnings for each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period`
                    AND facts's `cash earnings for the pay period` AT LEAST `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the amount of cash earnings` `the maximum weekly insurable earnings` TIMES n)   -- (b)(i)
                OR (    facts's `employment in each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period`
                    AND facts's `total number of hours of employment in the pay period` AT LEAST 15 TIMES n)   -- (b)(ii)
             THEN JUST n
             ELSE NOTHING
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Part II item 4 -- section 34: dependants (applies 30 June 1996 to 4 January 1997)`

-- src:2318 | 34 (1) A dependant of a claimant or of the spouse of a claimant is a person who is related to the claimant or the spouse in the manner described in subsection 251(6) of the Income Tax Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part II s 34(1) (src:2318)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `is related to the claimant or the spouse in the manner described in subsection 251(6) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the Income Tax Act (no piece: not among the inputs)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch III Part II s 34(1) the person is a dependant of the claimant or of the spouse of the claimant` IF
        `reg 95(5) the provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c) on the day` day
    AND `is related to the claimant or the spouse in the manner described in subsection 251(6) of the Income Tax Act`

-- src:2319 | (2) The spouse of a claimant is the person who is married to the claimant, and includes a person described in subsection 252(4) of the Income Tax Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part II s 34(2) (src:2319)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `is married to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a person described in subsection 252(4) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the Income Tax Act (no piece: not among the inputs)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch III Part II s 34(2) the person is the spouse of the claimant` IF
        `reg 95(5) the provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c) on the day` day
    AND (`is married to the claimant` OR `is a person described in subsection 252(4) of the Income Tax Act`)

-- src:2320 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph 14(1)(b) of the Act as set out in section 6 of Schedule II to the Act, the following circumstances are prescribed as circumstances which must exist in relation to one or more dependants of a claimant or of the spouse of the claimant:
-- src:2321 | (a) a child tax benefit as provided for in section 122.61 of the Income Tax Act is payable to either the claimant or the spouse during the month in which the claimant makes a claim for the benefit rate prescribed by paragraph 14(1)(b) of the Act as set out in section 6 of Schedule II to the Act; or
-- src:2322 | (b) the claimant or the spouse provides support to a dependant of the claimant or of the spouse of the claimant.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part II s 34(3) (src:2320-2322)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `a child tax benefit under section 122.61 of the Income Tax Act is payable to the claimant or the spouse during the month in which the claimant makes a claim for the benefit rate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant or the spouse provides support to a dependant of the claimant or of the spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch III Part II s 34(3) the circumstances prescribed for paragraph 14(1)(b) of the Act exist` IF
        `reg 95(5) the provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c) on the day` day
    AND (   `a child tax benefit under section 122.61 of the Income Tax Act is payable to the claimant or the spouse during the month in which the claimant makes a claim for the benefit rate`   -- (a)
         OR `the claimant or the spouse provides support to a dependant of the claimant or of the spouse`)   -- (b)

