§ `Part II item 6 -- paragraph 93(1)(c): weeks instead of hours (applies 30 June 1996 to 4 January 1997)`

-- src:2368 | 6 The following applies in place of paragraph 93(1)(c):
-- src:2369 | (c) has had 20 or more weeks of insurable employment in their qualifying period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule III Part II item 6, paragraph 93(1)(c) (src:2368-2369)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `weeks of insurable employment in the qualifying period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch III Part II item 6 paragraph 93(1)(c) the insured person has had 20 or more weeks of insurable employment in the qualifying period` IF
        `reg 95(5) the provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c) on the day` day
    AND `weeks of insurable employment in the qualifying period` AT LEAST 20
